when you make an http call you only have one response since it's not a stream unless specified. Since I'm making a get request `http.get('/api/todos').map(res => res.json());` the response is complete once I get my first result.

``` es6
var todoSubscription = this.http.get('/api/todos').
      filter(res => res.status >= 200 && res.status < 300).
      map(res => res.json());
todoSubscription.subscribe(
  value =>  console.log('next', value),
  err => {
    debugger;
    console.log('err', err)
  },
  complete => {
    debugger;
    console.log('complete', complete)
  }
);
```

the observable should fire the onComplete unless I map to `res.arrayBuffer()` which returns `ArrayBuffer`s then it would fire onComplete until it's done.

[xhr_backend.ts#L38](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/master/modules/angular2/src/http/backends/xhr_backend.ts#L38)

